Certainly! Below is a simple HTML and JavaScript script to create a form that accepts user input and saves it. For the purpose of this example, we'll assume that "saving" the text means storing it in a local variable (since there's no server-side functionality provided). If you want to save the data to a database or a file, you would need to set up a backend service.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Save User Input</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 50px;
        }
        .form-container {
            max-width: 400px;
            margin: auto;
        }
        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }
        input[type="text"] {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 8px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="form-container">
    <h2>Enter Your Text</h2>
    <form id="saveForm">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="userText">Text:</label>
            <input type="text" id="userText" name="userText" required>
        </div>
        <button type="submit">Save</button>
    </form>

    <p id="savedText"></p>
</div>

<script>
    document.getElementById('saveForm').addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
        event.preventDefault(); // Prevent the default form submission

        const userInput = document.getElementById('userText').value;

        if (userInput) {
            document.getElementById('savedText').innerText = `Your saved text: ${userInput}`;
        } else {
            alert('Please enter some text.');
        }
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Structure**:
   - A simple form with an input field and a submit button.
   - A paragraph (`<p>`) where the saved text will be displayed.

2. **CSS Styling**:
   - Basic styling to make the form look presentable.

3. **JavaScript Functionality**:
   - An event listener is added to the form's `submit` event.
   - When the form is submitted, the default action is prevented.
   - The value entered by the user is retrieved from the input field.
   - If the input is not empty, the text is displayed in the paragraph below the form.
   - If the input is empty, an alert prompts the user to enter some text.

This script provides a basic implementation and can be expanded to include more features such as validation, error handling, and more complex saving mechanisms depending on your requirements.

